<description>
Recover the repeating background pattern hidden under the largest solid rectangle.

Input structure:
- The grid is covered by a small row/column periodic pattern.
- Several non-pattern colors form solid rectangular foreground objects that
  overwrite the pattern.
- The requested output region is the largest of those solid rectangles.

Rule:
- Find every 4-connected monochromatic object whose bounding box is a filled
  rectangle with both dimensions greater than one.
- Treat those rectangles as masks, infer the smallest repeating tile that is
  consistent with all remaining visible pixels, and repaint the largest
  rectangle's coordinates with that tile.

Key insight: The rectangle colors are occluders; the visible pixels outside
them are enough to reconstruct the original periodic background underneath.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "symmetry/pattern",
  "src": "visible periodic background outside the solid rectangular occluders",
  "dst": "region covered by the largest solid rectangular occluder",
  "transform": "infer the minimal repeating tile from unoccluded pixels and output the tile values that would occupy the largest rectangle's coordinates",
  "grid_shape": "same shape as the largest rectangle"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 19-23 rows x 19-22 cols
  background:
    type: periodic tile covering entire grid
    tile_size: 3x3 or 4x4 (3x3 in 3/4 examples)
    tile_colors: 3-4 distinct colors
    constraint: tile colors must NOT form any solid rectangle (h>1, w>1) in the background [observed]
  occluders:
    count: 2-3 solid monochromatic rectangles
    colors: each uses a unique color NOT in the tile palette; all occluder colors are distinct
    dimensions: each side 3-12, area 9-100
    largest_unique: exactly one rectangle has strictly the largest area (target)
    placement: non-overlapping; no pixel overlap between any pair
    total_coverage: 18-33% of grid area
    visibility: every tile residue (r%rp, c%cp) must have >= 1 representative outside all occluders
  output:
    content: the tile pattern that would fill the largest rectangle's bounding box
    size: matches largest rectangle dimensions exactly

generation_strategy:
